Given an input x ∈ R^{ℓ×d}, a generic Hyena operator performs the following transformation:
q_s^c = ∑_{s'} T_{ss'}^{c} ∑_{c'} x_{s'}^{c'} W^{c'c}
k_s^c = ∑_{s'} H_{ss'}^{c} ∑_{c'} x_{s'}^{c'} U^{c'c}
v_s^c = ∑_{s'} K_{ss'}^{c} ∑_{c'} x_{s'}^{c'} P^{c'c}
y_s^c = ∑_{c'} ( q_s^{c'} [ ∑_{s'} G_{ss'}^{c'} k_{s'}^{c'} ] v_s^{c'} ) M^{c'c}
where W, U, P, M ∈ R^{d×d} are parametrized as dense or low-rank matrices, and T, H, K, G ∈ R^{ℓ×ℓ} are Toeplitz matrices corresponding to convolutions with the filters h_T, h_H, h_K, h_G, respectively.
